  "id": "DrugBank_DB00190 - MONDO_10709",
  "verbalization": "Carbidopa is implicated in the pathogenesis of Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome through its association with Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism, a condition that is itself linked to the syndrome. The evidence suggests that Carbidopa may act as a mediator in the development of this disorder, as it is indicated in multiple pathways leading to the syndrome. These pathways involve Carbidopa's role in the treatment of Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism, which in turn is associated with the syndrome. The shared indication of Carbidopa with Entacapone and Rasagiline further supports the notion that Carbidopa may influence the underlying pathophysiology of the syndrome through a common mechanism, possibly involving the dopamine system. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Carbidopa to contribute to the manifestation of Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
